---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '@bundu/ui/Section.astro';
import SectionHeader from '@bundu/ui/SectionHeader.astro';
import { Card } from '@bundu/ui/ui/card';
import { Button } from '@bundu/ui/ui/button';
import SovereigntyDiagram from '../../components/SovereigntyDiagram.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Blueprint — how Shamwari is built · Shamwari AI"
  description="Cloud, Ground and Mind; the two rules that must not be broken; and where Shamwari sits in the Bundu Ecosystem."
>
  <Section space="tight">
    <SectionHeader
      as="h1"
      size="display"
      eyebrow="Blueprint"
      title="How Shamwari is built"
      description="Shamwari isn't one model behind an API — it's three, and which one answers a question depends on whose question it is."
      max="max-w-2xl"
    />
  </Section>

  <Section bg="secondary" border>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      <Card padding="lg">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h4 text-foreground">Cloud</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Runs on routed third-party models. Fast, general knowledge, no
          persistent memory of you. Handles anything that isn't about your
          own life.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card padding="lg">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h4 text-foreground">Ground</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">
          The Zimbabwean corpus — law, tax, regulation — kept fresh and cited
          by section. What makes an answer <em>correct</em> instead of just
          fluent.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card padding="lg">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h4 text-foreground">Mind</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">
          A small, open-weight model that runs on your own device. The only
          thing that ever sees your personal data, because it never has to
          leave.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Data sovereignty" title="The two rules that must not be broken" max="max-w-2xl" />
    <SovereigntyDiagram class="mt-8">
      A question about your own life is answered on your device by Shamwari
      Mind. It is checked twice — once at the edge, once in the service that
      owns the data — because a leak here isn't an outage, it's a broken
      promise.
    </SovereigntyDiagram>

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6">
        <p class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-semibold text-foreground">
          <span class="flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-caption text-primary-foreground">1</span>
          Your personal data never reaches a third-party model
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Not the cloud providers we route to, not anyone. If a question is
          about your own life and the only available answer would mean
          sending it to an outside model, Shamwari says so and stops — it
          does not quietly answer with a shrug instead.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6">
        <p class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-semibold text-foreground">
          <span class="flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-caption text-primary-foreground">2</span>
          Only open-weight output trains Shamwari Mind
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">
          The model we train and give away is never built from output whose
          licence forbids that. Every exchange is labelled the moment it's
          generated, and the training pipeline physically cannot ingest
          anything labelled otherwise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6">
      <Button href="https://docs.shamwari.ai/rules/" external variant="ghost" arrow>
        Read the full technical detail
      </Button>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section bg="secondary" border>
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Ground — the moat" title="Freshness beats volume" max="max-w-2xl" />
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-body text-muted-foreground">
      A grounded small model beats an ungrounded large one on "what is the
      current PAYE threshold" — because the large one is guessing from memory
      and the small one is reading. Ground is a living corpus with an
      effective date on every document, not a one-time scrape: when a
      Statutory Instrument supersedes an older one, retrieval stops citing
      the repealed version.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-body text-muted-foreground">
      What people actually ask becomes the roadmap for what we ingest next,
      starting with law, then tax and monetary policy, then agriculture and
      health once the sourcing is right.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="Ecosystem"
      title="Where Shamwari sits in the Bundu Ecosystem"
      description="Bundu Foundation is a Zimbabwe-registered non-profit that holds the Shamwari IP and governs the wider ecosystem. Shamwari is sold commercially under Nyuchi Africa; the code itself stays Apache-2.0."
      max="max-w-2xl"
    />
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground">Bundu Labs</h3><p class="mt-1 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">Research.</p></div>
      <div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground">Mukoko</h3><p class="mt-1 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">The consumer super-app — several sub-apps currently running in beta.</p></div>
      <div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground">Nyuchi Africa</h3><p class="mt-1 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">The commercial pillar. Shamwari's paid tiers run here.</p></div>
      <div class="card border-2 border-primary bg-sodalite-container p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground">Shamwari AI</h3><p class="mt-1 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">The community pillar — this site.</p></div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
